{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Who says of his father.</b> In the matter of the calf." "<b>And he did not acknowledge his sons, for they observed Your word.</b> He did not treat his sons' lives as paramount in the wilderness, in order to observe Your word — this being the commandment of circumcising the sons — even though many of them died, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Yevamot 72b): ״מִפְּנֵי שֶׁלֹּא נָשְׁבָה לָהֶם רוּחַ צְפוֹנִית״ (because no north wind blew for them)." "<b>And Your covenant they preserved.</b> As the Sages of blessed memory said: the tribe of Levi did not serve idolatry, and this was verified in Egypt and in the wilderness."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "Resolved זִכְרוֹנָם לִבְרָכָה as 'of blessed memory' referring to the Sages (חז\"ל), per Sforno's standard usage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:34.177791555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}